## On the job {.unnumbered}

::: callout-important
## Why this matters day to day

Any time you're asked to rank people-metrics across managers, teams,
stores, or offices of different sizes — attrition, engagement,
complaints, absence, sales per head — this chapter's approach applies
directly. Publishing the raw league table is the single most common
statistical mistake in People Analytics reporting, and it's an easy one
to fix once you know to look for it: check whether the extremes cluster
among the smallest groups. If they do, shrink before you share.
:::

